# Rocci language reference

A `.rocci` file is a Roc module with explicit template and server declarations.
Everything outside recognized declarations stays Roc.

## File structure

```rocci
module Example exposing [card]

import Html

Tone : [Neutral, Positive]

label = |tone| ...

@component Card = |{ title }|
    <article><h2>{title}</h2></article>
```

Recognized top-level forms are `@component`, `@fixture`, `@css`, `@context`,
`@init`, and `@on`.

## Components

```text
@component Name = |params| html
@component Name = |params| { template }
```

Component names are PascalCase. Lowered Roc values use lower camel case:
`StatusCard` becomes `statusCard`. One root tag needs no braces; multiple roots,
directives, or preamble items use a braced body.

An additional parameter receives the paired tag body:

```rocci
@component Badge = |{ tone }, content|
    <span class={toneClass(tone)}>{content}</span>
```

## Tags

| Form | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `<div>` | Intrinsic HTML element |
| `<Hello />` | Local component call |
| `<Design.Button />` | Qualified component call |
| `<>...</>` | Fragment |
| `<br>` or `<img />` | Void HTML element |

Unknown PascalCase tags lower to calls and are reported later by the Roc compiler.

## Attributes

| Form | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `class="card"` | Static string |
| `class={cardClass(state)}` | Roc expression |
| `disabled` | Boolean attribute |
| `data-on:click=@post("/actions/x")` | Datastar backend action |

Attribute names may contain hyphens. Prop spreading and dynamic attribute names
are not supported.

## Text and interpolation

`{expr}` in text position must produce a `Str`, unless it is a bare component
body parameter already typed as `Html`. Convert numbers at the interpolation
site, for example `{count.to_str()}`.

## Directives

| Directive | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `@let name = expr` | Bind a Roc value before render-producing items |
| `@if condition { ... }` | Render structural branches |
| `@for item in items { ... }` | Map a list to template items |
| `@match value { Pattern => ... }` | Pattern-match structural branches |
| `@css { ... }` | Add raw scoped CSS |

The body-opening `{` must be on the logical directive header line. Markup is
not allowed inside an arbitrary Roc expression.

## Fixtures

```rocci
@fixture{target: TodoItem}
todoItemExample = { item: { id: 1, text: "Buy milk" } }
```

The fixture remains a normal Roc binding and is indexed for preview tools.
Unqualified targets must name a local component.

## Server declarations

```rocci
@context { db : Sqlite.Db }
@init { ... }
@on:get("/") = |{ db }| { ... }
@on:post("/actions/save") = |{ db }| { ... }
```

These forms apply to standalone apps. Bodies are Roc. `@context` declares
state, `@init` creates it, and `@on` defines route handlers.

## Comments and escaping

- `#` begins a template line comment at the start of an item.
- `<!-- ... -->` is dropped as an HTML comment.
- `@@` emits a literal `@` inside a template body.
- Ordinary Roc comments remain valid in Roc regions.

## Deliberate limits

Rocci does not provide arbitrary JSX, dynamic tags, prop spreading, a runtime
component registry, or markup embedded in arbitrary Roc expressions.
